                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dd1a1dd7-294e-3754-bbc8-dd2c46009bab",
                        "entry_id": "430b8ac2-f07a-3656-b183-6d0189bacdb9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. уменьш. к семья"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d2891c5-caf7-3b63-a5b2-d4a77df9a2a7",
                        "entry_id": "430b8ac2-f07a-3656-b183-6d0189bacdb9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "пренебр. к семья"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe665489-6e7a-4414-929b-341b99a0ceed",
                                "sense_id": "9d2891c5-caf7-3b63-a5b2-d4a77df9a2a7",
                                "text": "Надо вам сказать, что вся наша семейка, как и прежде семейка Рахленко, не отличалась особенной благовоспитанностью: здоровые, отчаянные, первые драчуны и забияки."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "14b060b1-1280-4845-a250-a007c8ae87e6",
                        "source_entry_id": "430b8ac2-f07a-3656-b183-6d0189bacdb9",
                        "target_lang_word": "family",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "family",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88635fb1-ae8f-39cb-a8fc-127ff03632f9",
                                        "entry_id": "6a85e7b6-f6b4-3741-858f-c49774296b04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of people who are closely related to one another (by blood, marriage or adoption); kin; in particular, a set of parents and their children; an immediate family."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcdb179c-0c7a-46bd-a381-abf14b385ada",
                                                "sense_id": "88635fb1-ae8f-39cb-a8fc-127ff03632f9",
                                                "text": "Our family lives in town."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b329d96-6387-47e7-bfba-f45ae62640a0",
                                                "sense_id": "88635fb1-ae8f-39cb-a8fc-127ff03632f9",
                                                "text": "To Jane, he could be only a man whose proposals she had refused, and whose merit she had undervalued; but to her own more extensive information, he was the person, to whom the whole family were indebted for the first of benefits, and whom she regarded herself with an interest, if not quite so tender, at least as reasonable and just, as what Jane felt for Bingley."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72ccb452-7856-499e-8b3e-537637c60a81",
                                                "sense_id": "88635fb1-ae8f-39cb-a8fc-127ff03632f9",
                                                "text": "Such a scandal as the prosecution of a brother for forgery—with a verdict of guilty—is a most truly horrible, deplorable, fatal thing. It takes the respectability out of a family perhaps at a critical moment, when the family is just assuming the robes of respectability:[…]it is a black spot which all the soaps ever advertised could never wash off."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81042c06-87cb-47ff-97b5-da0c9bdaff99",
                                                "sense_id": "88635fb1-ae8f-39cb-a8fc-127ff03632f9",
                                                "text": "America’s poverty line is $63 a day for a family of four. In the richer parts of the emerging world $4 a day is the poverty barrier. But poverty’s scourge is fiercest below $1.25 ([…]): people below that level live lives that are poor, nasty, brutish and short."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b28d008-7c27-415e-8f86-1f4d1d9f30e2",
                                                "sense_id": "88635fb1-ae8f-39cb-a8fc-127ff03632f9",
                                                "text": "They’re both New Yorkers coasting on their reputations, they’ve both had three marriages, neither of them can shut up when in front of a camera, and perhaps most importantly, they both want to fuck Ivanka, which-which is weird for Trump because Ivanka is in his family, and it’s weird for Giuliani because she isn’t."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "990051ae-8742-3d92-9dbd-fc2bfe803f4f",
                                        "entry_id": "6a85e7b6-f6b4-3741-858f-c49774296b04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An extended family: a group of people who are related to one another by blood or marriage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "650a9324-bf21-3268-a468-a227403ee487",
                                        "entry_id": "6a85e7b6-f6b4-3741-858f-c49774296b04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A nuclear family: a mother and father who are married and cohabiting and their child or children."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d7dc67b-6164-43c8-8036-be629b2fb17b",
                                                "sense_id": "650a9324-bf21-3268-a468-a227403ee487",
                                                "text": "We must preserve the family unit if we want to save civilisation!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccede233-fefd-45b7-9e47-e153d61ef2a1",
                                                "sense_id": "650a9324-bf21-3268-a468-a227403ee487",
                                                "text": "The cultural struggle is for the survival of family values against all manner of atheistic amorality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7eb2912b-c66d-32d6-8dc7-6d93a057814f",
                                        "entry_id": "6a85e7b6-f6b4-3741-858f-c49774296b04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Members of one's family collectively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33c1e669-7ff3-48ac-969e-4c403348327a",
                                                "sense_id": "7eb2912b-c66d-32d6-8dc7-6d93a057814f",
                                                "text": "I have a lot of family in Australia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6add1c22-edff-44ba-a088-bdee7cdcf6c4",
                                                "sense_id": "7eb2912b-c66d-32d6-8dc7-6d93a057814f",
                                                "text": "He has a sister, but no other family."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76f50689-8762-38cf-8331-5e4ab9a18038",
                                        "entry_id": "6a85e7b6-f6b4-3741-858f-c49774296b04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A (close-knit) group of people related by blood, friendship, marriage, law, or custom, especially if they live or work together."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddf2e099-f4cf-4060-b89b-b537d352162e",
                                                "sense_id": "76f50689-8762-38cf-8331-5e4ab9a18038",
                                                "text": "crime family, Mafia family"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "608b1ad2-e333-45ca-8eb0-763c2bfb37c6",
                                                "sense_id": "76f50689-8762-38cf-8331-5e4ab9a18038",
                                                "text": "This is my fraternity family at the university."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7e2df7b-c239-4d34-88e1-e0dddf086a19",
                                                "sense_id": "76f50689-8762-38cf-8331-5e4ab9a18038",
                                                "text": "Our company is one big happy family."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de7b72ab-d944-3a0e-827b-30a415258d10",
                                        "entry_id": "6a85e7b6-f6b4-3741-858f-c49774296b04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A (close-knit) group of people related by blood, friendship, marriage, law, or custom, especially if they live or work together.",
                                            "The gay community."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec7ff72f-49e2-4134-823a-7f2c03ef6953",
                                                "sense_id": "de7b72ab-d944-3a0e-827b-30a415258d10",
                                                "text": "[…]This is not your hallmark im Ames, Iowa. And there is “family” working there . . . no radar like gaydar, I always say."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a1acfa7b-e0d3-369f-8955-4341b75288d4",
                                        "entry_id": "6a85e7b6-f6b4-3741-858f-c49774296b04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lineage, especially honorable or noble lineage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9141f41-776e-4f6e-b391-678e9a9f5f29",
                                                "sense_id": "a1acfa7b-e0d3-369f-8955-4341b75288d4",
                                                "text": "Indeed, he married her for love. A whisper still goes about that she had not even 'family'; howbeit, Sir Leicester had so much family that perhaps he had enough and could dispense with any more."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "536ec9c1-5115-377e-badb-6ec7302cc34d",
                                        "entry_id": "6a85e7b6-f6b4-3741-858f-c49774296b04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any group or aggregation of things classed together as kindred or related from possessing in common characteristics which distinguish them from other things of the same order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e514582b-3383-43ee-8fbc-ab5513a3c9d9",
                                                "sense_id": "536ec9c1-5115-377e-badb-6ec7302cc34d",
                                                "text": "Doliracetam is a drug from the racetam family."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "304c0fa0-2e90-4b8a-906a-88d64e893140",
                                                "sense_id": "536ec9c1-5115-377e-badb-6ec7302cc34d",
                                                "text": "When creating a font family, first decide whether to use all serif or all sans-serif fonts, then choose two or three fonts of that type […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "658c8a0f-5781-409b-a958-e50025288120",
                                                "sense_id": "536ec9c1-5115-377e-badb-6ec7302cc34d",
                                                "text": "Of the great Indo-European family of languages the general principal was also that of one name for each individual[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47206fb0-ff97-32ff-8f71-9e2b7f891e7b",
                                        "entry_id": "6a85e7b6-f6b4-3741-858f-c49774296b04",
